85df0702-6585-41ba-a16c-282e21d1a4f9	2f4db866-fd7a-47f2-bc50-f5169e8f8736	Writ me short cultural story in amharic	የአስተማሪ ታሪክ\n\nበዚህ ታሪክ ላይ የአማርኛ ባህል የተሰማሩ ልጆች እና ልጆቻቸው የሚገኙ የአማርኛ ባህሎች የሚወጡ የአማርኛ ባህሎች እንዲሁም የአማርኛ ባህሎች የሚወጡ ሌሎች ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። የአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማርኛ ቋንቋ የሚናገሩት አንድ የሚሰማሩ ባህሎች ናቸው። \n\nአማርኛ ባህሎች በአማ	2084
39f917cb-c512-4d98-95a8-3bd78d5a7fed	2f4db866-fd7a-47f2-bc50-f5169e8f8736	Writ me short cultural story in amharic	የአማርኛ ታሪክ: የአስተማሪ ስብስብ\n\nበዚህ ታሪክ የአማርኛ ባህል ስብስብ የሚለውን የአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክን ይጠብቁ። የአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክ ከሰማይ እንደሚገኝ የሚያስተምር ነው።\n\nበዚህ ታሪክ የአስተማሪ ስብስብ አዲስ አበባ በአማርኛ ማስተማር ላይ ተገኝቶ በሚያስተምር ጊዜ አስተማሪ ስብስብ የሚለውን ስብስብ ታሪክ ይጠብቁ።\n\nአዲስ አበባው በአማርኛ ማስተማር ላይ ተገኝቶ በሚያስተምር ጊዜ የአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክ ይጠብቁ።\n\nአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክ:\n\nበዚህ ታሪክ የአስተማሪ ስብስብ አዲስ አበባ በአማርኛ ማስተማር ላይ ተገኝቶ በሚያስተምር ጊዜ አስተማሪ ስብስብ የሚለውን ስብስብ ታሪክ ይጠብቁ።\n\nአዲስ አበባው በአማርኛ ማስተማር ላይ ተገኝቶ በሚያስተምር ጊዜ የአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክ ይጠብቁ።\n\nአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክ:\n\nበዚህ ታሪክ የአስተማሪ ስብስብ አዲስ አበባ በአማርኛ ማስተማር ላይ ተገኝቶ በሚያስተምር ጊዜ አስተማሪ ስብስብ የሚለውን ስብስብ ታሪክ ይጠብቁ።\n\nአዲስ አበባው በአማርኛ ማስተማር ላይ ተገኝቶ በሚያስተምር ጊዜ የአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክ ይጠብቁ።\n\nአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክ:\n\nበዚህ ታሪክ የአስተማሪ ስብስብ አዲስ አበባ በአማርኛ ማስተማር ላይ ተገኝቶ በሚያስተምር ጊዜ አስተማሪ ስብስብ የሚለውን ስብስብ ታሪክ ይጠብቁ።\n\nአዲስ አበባው በአማርኛ ማስተማር ላይ ተገኝቶ በሚያስተምር ጊዜ የአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክ ይጠብቁ።\n\nአስተማሪ ስብስብ ታሪክ:\n\nበዚህ ታሪክ የአስተማሪ ስብስብ አዲስ አበባ በአማርኛ ማስተማር ላይ ተገኝቶ በሚያስተም	2083
778ae057-c5d6-4412-ac39-909e4b02e559	6d5c9ccf-5e07-4eb2-95ee-b6e9cfbf921d	hi	Hello! How can I assist you today?	37
c47e6587-b128-4e6d-ad9a-0adc0cd3f95f	bed6b161-85bf-4c7f-90c5-32b4f36dc70e	What is angle of attack in airplane	The angle of attack (AOA) in an airplane refers to the angle between the oncoming airflow and the reference line of the aircraft's wing. It is a crucial parameter that determines the lift and drag forces acting on the aircraft. A higher angle of attack increases lift but also increases drag. However, if the angle of attack becomes too high, it can lead to a stall, where the airflow over the wing becomes disrupted and lift is greatly reduced. Pilots must carefully manage the angle of attack during different phases of flight to ensure safe and efficient operation of the aircraft.	149
2e52c754-1787-4b32-88fc-3ffeb1fc8086	bed6b161-85bf-4c7f-90c5-32b4f36dc70e	What is the difference between aircraft and airplane	The terms "aircraft" and "airplane" are often used interchangeably, but there is a slight difference between the two.\n\nAn aircraft is a general term that refers to any vehicle that is capable of flying in the Earth's atmosphere. It includes a wide range of vehicles, such as airplanes, helicopters, gliders, and even drones.\n\nOn the other hand, an airplane specifically refers to a fixed-wing aircraft that is powered by engines and is designed for carrying passengers or cargo through the air. Airplanes have wings that generate lift, allowing them to stay airborne, and they are typically used for transportation over long distances.\n\nIn summary, while all airplanes are aircraft, not all aircraft are airplanes. Airplanes are a specific type of aircraft that have fixed wings and are powered by engines for the purpose of transporting people or goods through the air.	205
be2506e8-0a39-4aa2-af12-befcfc46bda6	bed6b161-85bf-4c7f-90c5-32b4f36dc70e	How a plane lands	A plane lands through a series of carefully coordinated steps performed by the pilot and the aircraft's systems. Here's a simplified explanation of the landing process:\n\n1. Approach: The pilot begins the landing process by initiating the descent towards the destination airport. The plane follows a designated flight path, guided by air traffic control.\n\n2. Flaps and Landing Gear: As the plane descends, the pilot extends the flaps and landing gear. Flaps are movable surfaces on the wings that increase lift and drag, allowing the plane to maintain a slower speed during landing. The landing gear is lowered to provide stability and support during touchdown.\n\n3. Final Approach: The plane enters the final approach phase, aligning with the runway. The pilot adjusts the throttle and controls the plane's pitch, roll, and yaw to maintain a stable descent.\n\n4. Glide Slope and Localizer: The pilot uses instruments, such as the glide slope and localizer, to ensure proper alignment with the runway. The glide slope provides vertical guidance, while the localizer provides horizontal guidance.\n\n5. Touchdown: As the plane nears the runway, the pilot reduces the throttle to decrease speed. The main wheels make contact with the runway, followed by the nose wheel. The pilot maintains control and applies brakes to slow down the plane.\n\n6. Rollout: After touchdown, the pilot continues to steer the plane using the rudder pedals. The flaps are gradually retracted, and the brakes are applied as needed to bring the plane to a complete stop.\n\nIt's important to note that the landing process can vary depending on factors such as weather conditions, aircraft type, and airport procedures. Pilots undergo extensive training and follow specific protocols to ensure safe and smooth landings.	381
ba187ec9-244a-4ad4-a088-4f908871cffd	bed6b161-85bf-4c7f-90c5-32b4f36dc70e	Jet engine types	There are several types of jet engines used in aviation. Here are some of the most common ones:\n\n1. Turbojet Engine: This is the simplest type of jet engine, consisting of a compressor, combustion chamber, turbine, and nozzle. It compresses incoming air, mixes it with fuel, ignites the mixture, and then expels the hot gases through the nozzle to produce thrust.\n\n2. Turbofan Engine: Also known as a fanjet, this type of engine is commonly used in commercial aircraft. It has an additional fan at the front, which bypasses some of the air around the combustion chamber. This bypass air provides additional thrust and improves fuel efficiency.\n\n3. Turboprop Engine: This type of engine is used in smaller aircraft and regional airliners. It combines a gas turbine engine with a propeller. The turbine powers the propeller, which generates most of the thrust. Turboprop engines are known for their efficiency at lower speeds and altitudes.\n\n4. Turbo shaft Engine: Similar to a turboprop engine, a turboshaft engine also uses a gas turbine to drive a shaft. However, instead of driving a propeller, the shaft is used to power various devices, such as helicopters' rotor systems or auxiliary power units (APUs) in aircraft.\n\n5. Ramjet Engine: Unlike other jet engines, a ramjet engine does not have any moving parts. It relies on the forward motion of the aircraft to compress incoming air. The compressed air is then mixed with fuel and ignited to produce thrust. Ramjets are most efficient at high speeds.\n\n6. Scramjet Engine: Similar to a ramjet, a scramjet engine operates at hypersonic speeds (above Mach 5). It compresses incoming air using shockwaves generated by the high-speed airflow. Scramjets are still in experimental stages and have potential applications in hypersonic flight and space exploration.\n\nThese are just a few examples of jet engine types, and there are variations and combinations of these engines used in different aircraft depending on their specific requirements.	444
8fc4d4de-fc9f-484e-8f90-a35b4d8608bd	bed6b161-85bf-4c7f-90c5-32b4f36dc70e	Group discussion ideas on the impact of peer pressure	1. The role of peer pressure in shaping individual behavior and decision-making.\n2. The positive and negative effects of peer pressure on personal development.\n3. How peer pressure can influence academic performance and study habits.\n4. The impact of peer pressure on mental health and self-esteem.\n5. Exploring strategies to resist negative peer pressure and make independent choices.\n6. The influence of social media and online communities on peer pressure dynamics.\n7. The role of parents, teachers, and mentors in mitigating the negative effects of peer pressure.\n8. The connection between peer pressure and risky behaviors such as substance abuse or bullying.\n9. Examining cultural and societal factors that contribute to peer pressure dynamics.\n10. The long-term consequences of succumbing to peer pressure versus staying true to oneself.	193
