5c0b110a-c768-4c6d-a221-3ba87024b025	3302be8d-ffda-49a0-997c-b5a2adec54e1	Which organelle is responsible for the synthesis of lipids and detoxification of harmful substances in the cell?	The organelle responsible for the synthesis of lipids and detoxification of harmful substances in the cell is the endoplasmic reticulum (ER). There are two types of ER: rough endoplasmic reticulum (RER) and smooth endoplasmic reticulum (SER). The RER is involved in protein synthesis, while the SER is responsible for lipid synthesis and detoxification processes.	134
a166766f-1b90-47ac-a20c-ae6b0fb7c0ee	3302be8d-ffda-49a0-997c-b5a2adec54e1	Name the organelle that contain enzymes responsible for intracellular digestion?	The organelle that contains enzymes responsible for intracellular digestion is called the lysosome.	59
ad32aa8b-62cb-4332-b6ef-3525070ca0e8	3302be8d-ffda-49a0-997c-b5a2adec54e1	What is the function of golgi apparatus in the cell?	The Golgi apparatus, also known as the Golgi complex or Golgi body, is an organelle found in eukaryotic cells. Its main function is to process, package, and distribute proteins and lipids that are synthesized by the cell.\n\nThe Golgi apparatus receives proteins and lipids from the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) in small transport vesicles. Once inside the Golgi apparatus, these molecules undergo a series of modifications. This includes the addition of carbohydrates (glycosylation), the sorting and packaging of proteins into vesicles, and the modification of lipids.\n\nThe Golgi apparatus consists of a series of flattened sacs called cisternae. Each cisterna has distinct regions: the cis-Golgi network (CGN), the medial-Golgi, and the trans-Golgi network (TGN). These regions have different enzymes and functions.\n\nAfter processing, the Golgi apparatus packages the modified proteins and lipids into vesicles for transport to their final destinations. Some vesicles are sent to the plasma membrane for secretion, while others are directed to other organelles within the cell.\n\nIn summary, the Golgi apparatus plays a crucial role in the post-translational modification, sorting, and packaging of proteins and lipids, ensuring their proper distribution within the cell and for secretion outside the cell.	314
56b6b572-2497-49af-b776-bd208d28fcca	3302be8d-ffda-49a0-997c-b5a2adec54e1	What is the function of golgi apparatus in the cell? Shortly	The Golgi apparatus, also known as the Golgi complex or Golgi body, is an organelle found in eukaryotic cells. Its main function is to process, package, and distribute proteins and lipids that are synthesized by the cell. It receives these molecules from the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) and modifies them by adding sugars, lipids, or other molecules to form functional proteins or lipids. The Golgi apparatus then packages these molecules into vesicles and sends them to their specific destinations within the cell or for secretion outside the cell. Additionally, the Golgi apparatus is involved in the synthesis of certain carbohydrates and the formation of lysosomes.	178
d8df3079-5cb4-4e9c-bd98-4ca94a6e4615	3302be8d-ffda-49a0-997c-b5a2adec54e1	Which organelle is responsible for generating energy in the form of ATP through cellular respiration?	The organelle responsible for generating energy in the form of ATP through cellular respiration is the mitochondria.	68
05fe66ac-afb4-4e13-8237-e4e32704732e	3302be8d-ffda-49a0-997c-b5a2adec54e1	Identify the organelle that plays a crucial role in maintaining cell shape, providing support, and facilitating cell movement	The organelle that plays a crucial role in maintaining cell shape, providing support, and facilitating cell movement is the cytoskeleton.	77
ba68f20a-e58c-4e6c-9e75-e538afea14b0	3302be8d-ffda-49a0-997c-b5a2adec54e1	What is the function of the nucleolus within the nucleus	The nucleolus is a distinct structure within the nucleus of a cell. Its main function is to assemble ribosomes, which are responsible for protein synthesis. The nucleolus contains DNA, RNA, and proteins, and it plays a crucial role in the production and processing of ribosomal RNA (rRNA). It also helps in the assembly of ribosomal subunits before they are transported out of the nucleus to the cytoplasm, where they can participate in protein synthesis. Additionally, the nucleolus is involved in regulating cell growth and proliferation.	149
7cac47fe-e187-4485-b0c7-880c7a0e8161	3302be8d-ffda-49a0-997c-b5a2adec54e1	What is the function of the nucleolus within the nucleus shrtly	The nucleolus is a distinct structure found within the nucleus of eukaryotic cells. Its main function is to assemble ribosomes, which are responsible for protein synthesis. The nucleolus contains DNA, RNA, and proteins, and it serves as a site for the synthesis and processing of ribosomal RNA (rRNA). Additionally, it also plays a role in the assembly of ribosomal subunits before they are transported out of the nucleus to the cytoplasm, where they can participate in protein synthesis.	145
