f1cc3012-da4e-41fc-9421-a36098714b0d	7bda5cee-7ef5-4d96-8c6c-1d09865b14a9	What is hypoxemia?	Hypoxemia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of oxygen in the blood. It occurs when there is insufficient oxygen reaching the body's tissues. This can be caused by various factors, such as lung diseases, heart problems, high altitudes, or certain medical conditions. Symptoms of hypoxemia may include shortness of breath, rapid breathing, confusion, dizziness, and cyanosis (bluish discoloration of the skin and mucous membranes). Treatment typically involves addressing the underlying cause and providing supplemental oxygen if necessary. It is important to seek medical attention if you suspect you have hypoxemia, as it can be a serious condition.	164
