c4a108e2-9bbf-4960-bfab-34e12092638e	10aa5488-d23a-487e-9794-a7fdb4812d7b	It's Ict assignment like html the list are \n Roman numbers 1 A) minimal page \nB) heading \nC) element\nD) list\nRoman numbers 2 .css internal\n. External\n. Inline\nThe third like table\nRoll numbers  name gender age\nRoll numbers 1 name bill gender m age 17\nRoman numbers 2 name lili gender m age 18\n Roman numbers 3 name merry gender f age 16\nCan you give me the tags please	Sure! Here are the HTML tags you can use for each item in your list:\n\nRoman numbers 1:\nA) minimal page: `<html>`, `<head>`, `<title>`, `<body>`\nB) heading: `<h1>`, `<h2>`, `<h3>`, `<h4>`, `<h5>`, `<h6>`\nC) element: `<div>`, `<span>`, `<p>`, `<a>`, `<img>`, `<input>`, `<button>`, etc.\nD) list: `<ul>`, `<ol>`, `<li>`\n\nRoman numbers 2:\n.css internal: `<style>`\nExternal: `<link>`\nInline: `<style>`\n\nThe third item - table:\nTo create a table, you can use the following tags:\n`<table>`: Defines the start of the table.\n`<tr>`: Defines a row in the table.\n`<th>`: Defines a header cell in a table.\n`<td>`: Defines a standard cell in a table.\n\nHere's an example of how you can use these tags to create the table you mentioned:\n\n```html\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Roll numbers</th>\n    <th>Name</th>\n    <th>Gender</th>\n    <th>Age</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>1</td>\n    <td>Bill</td>\n    <td>M</td>\n    <td>17</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>2</td>\n    <td>Lili</td>\n    <td>M</td>\n    <td>18</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>3</td>\n    <td>Merry</td>\n    <td>F</td>\n    <td>16</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n```\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.	544
a05ee330-9b2d-4f96-a08a-1c72fc7774dd	10aa5488-d23a-487e-9794-a7fdb4812d7b	Like html tr tag oi tag and so many tag	Yes, HTML has many tags that serve different purposes. The `<tr>` tag is used to define a row in an HTML table. It is typically used in conjunction with the `<table>` and `<td>` tags to create a structured table layout.\n\nThe `<oi>` tag, on the other hand, is not a standard HTML tag. It seems like you may have made a typo. If you meant the `<ol>` tag, it is used to create an ordered list in HTML. Each list item is defined using the `<li>` tag within the `<ol>` tag.\n\nHTML has a wide range of tags that can be used to structure and format content on a webpage. Some commonly used tags include `<p>` for paragraphs, `<h1>` to `<h6>` for headings, `<a>` for links, `<img>` for images, and many more.	212
