122750c9-c48d-4b06-9847-5ac1de53ff79	assistant	2023-12-03 12:23:18.985218	Certainly! Here's the algorithm to check if a number is prime or not, implemented in Python:\n\n```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_prime(n):\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    sqrt_n = int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1\n    for divisor in range(3, sqrt_n, 2):\n        if n % divisor == 0:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```\n\nYou can use the `is_prime()` function to check if a number is prime or not. It returns `True` if the number is prime and `False` otherwise.\n\nFor example, you can call the function like this:\n\n```python\nnumber = 37\nif is_prime(number):\n    print(f"{number} is a prime number.")\nelse:\n    print(f"{number} is not a prime number.")\n```\n\nThis will output: "37 is a prime number."\n\nFeel free to use this implementation in your Python programs. Let me know if there's anything else I can assist you with!	235	1e7298d1-e8e2-44cf-9e78-cfadb495fa08	2
