s techniques such as try-catch blocks and exception handling.\n\n10. Input/Output: Input/output (I/O) refers to the interaction between a program and its environment. It involves reading input from users or external sources and displaying output to users or storing it in external devices.\n\nThese are just a few examples of programming concepts. Understanding these concepts and applying them effectively is essential for writing clean, efficient, and functional code.	447	9a080ba6-a3d8-4d08-bd46-f2a1116fb210	1
