 to make informed decisions based on accurate and timely information. For example, a business intelligence system can consolidate data from sales, marketing, finance, and operations to generate reports, dashboards, and analytics. These insights help managers identify trends, evaluate performance, and make data-driven decisions. For instance, a marketing manager can analyze customer data to identify target segments, optimize marketing campaigns, and allocate resources effectively.\n\n4. Strategic Planning and Performance Measurement: Information systems support strategic planning and performance measurement by providing access to relevant data and performance metrics across different functional areas. For example, a balanced scorecard system integrates financial, customer, internal process, and learning and growth perspectives to measure and monitor organizational performance. This cross-functional approach ensures that strategic goals are aligned with operational activities and enables managers to track progress and make adjustments as needed.\n\n5. Customer-centric Approach: In today's customer-centric business environment, information systems help organizations gather, analyze, and utilize customer data across different functional areas. This enables a holistic view of the customer and supports personalized and targeted marketing, sales, and customer service efforts. For example, a customer data platform (CDP) integrates data from various touchpoints, such as website interactions, social media, and customer support, to create a unified customer profile. This profile can be accessed by marketing, sales, and customer service teams to provide personalized experiences and tailored offerings.\n\nIn summary, the applications of information systems have become cross-functional in today's business environment due to the integration of business processes, the need for real-time information sharing, the importance of data-driven decision-making, strategic planning and performance measurement, and the customer-centric approach. By leveraging information systems across functional areas, organizations can improve coordination, enhance decision-making, and deliver better customer experiences.	654	52f20d9f-5fa7-4c44-ab91-8b2bf7bb614e	1
