430d8dba-305c-4d7e-97bd-3b78ea452499	assistant	2023-09-19 13:16:13.403997	To check if a string is a number in Python, you can use the `isdigit()` method or a regular expression.\n\nHere's an example using the `isdigit()` method:\n\n```python\ndef is_number(string):\n    return string.isdigit()\n\n# Example usage\nprint(is_number("123"))  # True\nprint(is_number("abc"))  # False\n```\n\nAnd here's an example using a regular expression:\n\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef is_number(string):\n    pattern = r'^[-+]?[0-9]+$'\n    return re.match(pattern, string) is not None\n\n# Example usage\nprint(is_number("123"))  # True\nprint(is_number("-456"))  # True\nprint(is_number("abc"))  # False\n```\n\nBoth methods will return `True` if the string is a number, and `False` otherwise.	177	5029bc1b-55b3-41e0-a94c-ea917ed8a67f	1
