673793c2-7673-4d5e-b1df-554e4cd1ced5	assistant	2023-09-19 13:29:03.400684	To make your aiogram bot a serverless app and automatically get the URL from FastAPI, you can use the `vercel-python` package. Here's how you can do it:\n\n1. Install the required packages:\n   - Install the `vercel-python` package using pip:\n     ```\n     pip install vercel-python\n     ```\n\n2. Update your FastAPI app:\n   - Import the `vercel_python` module:\n     ```python\n     from vercel_python import VercelPython\n     ```\n\n   - Create an instance of the `VercelPython` class and pass your FastAPI app:\n     ```python\n     vercel = VercelPython(app)\n     ```\n\n   - Define a route for the webhook:\n     ```python\n     @app.post("/webhook")\n     async def webhook(request: types.Update):\n         await dp.process_update(request)\n         return "ok"\n     ```\n\n   - Run the FastAPI app using the `vercel.handle` method:\n     ```python\n     if __name__ == "__main__":\n         vercel.handle(app)\n     ```\n\n3. Deploy to Vercel:\n   - In your project directory, run the following command to deploy to Vercel:\n     ```\n     vercel\n     ```\n\n   - Follow the prompts to configure your deployment settings.\n   - Once the deployment is complete, Vercel will provide you with a URL for your deployed app.\n\n4. Set up the webhook in your aiogram bot:\n   - Use the URL provided by Vercel to set up the webhook in your aiogram bot:\n     ```python\n     from aiogram import Bot\n\n     bot = Bot(token="YOUR_BOT_TOKEN")\n     await bot.set_webhook(url="YOUR_VERCEL_APP_URL/webhook")\n     ```\n\n   - Replace "YOUR_BOT_TOKEN" with your actual bot token and "YOUR_VERCEL_APP_URL" with the URL provided by Vercel.\n\nWith this setup, the `vercel-python` package will automatically handle the deployment and URL generation for your FastAPI app. Your aiogram bot will be deployed as a serverless app on Vercel, and the webhook URL will be obtained dynamically.	452	980aed93-6686-4a07-a1e7-1ef65002f4a