nt settings.\n5. Once the deployment is complete, Vercel will provide you with a URL for your deployed app.\n\nStep 4: Set up the webhook in your aiogram bot\n1. Open your aiogram bot code.\n2. Import the `Bot` class from the `aiogram` module:\n   ```python\n   from aiogram import Bot\n   ```\n3. Create an instance of the `Bot` class with your bot token:\n   ```python\n   bot = Bot(token="YOUR_BOT_TOKEN")\n   ```\n   Replace "YOUR_BOT_TOKEN" with your actual bot token.\n4. Use the URL provided by Vercel to set up the webhook in your aiogram bot:\n   ```python\n   await bot.set_webhook(url="YOUR_VERCEL_APP_URL/webhook")\n   ```\n   Replace "YOUR_VERCEL_APP_URL" with the URL provided by Vercel.\n\nThat's it! Your aiogram bot should now be deployed to Vercel and using FastAPI for webhooking. Any incoming updates will be processed by your bot through the defined `/webhook` route.	709	980aed93-6686-4a07-a1e7-1ef65002f4a5	1
