21fd6f0f-a096-49f9-8a26-b5591155998e	assistant	2023-09-21 11:06:45.658935	To ensure that packets are not dropped due to excessive data transmission, a method called flow control can be used. Flow control allows two computers to regulate the rate at which data is sent and received to prevent congestion and packet loss.\n\nThere are two main types of flow control:\n\n1. Stop-and-Wait Flow Control: In this method, the sender sends a packet and waits for an acknowledgment (ACK) from the receiver before sending the next packet. This ensures that the receiver can handle the incoming data at its own pace and prevents overwhelming the receiver with too much data.\n\n2. Sliding Window Flow Control: This method allows the sender to send multiple packets without waiting for individual acknowledgments. The receiver specifies the size of its receive window, which indicates the number of packets it can accept at a given time. The sender can send packets up to the size of the receive window before waiting for acknowledgments. As the receiver processes the packets and sends acknowledgments, the sender can continue sending more packets within the window size.\n\nBoth methods help in maintaining a balanced flow of data between two computers, preventing packet loss due to excessive data transmission.	226	cd0327ee-4e9a-4d2c-94c6-b2eeaf459112	1
