8608a72c-c340-47f9-9618-680d9f524d5e	assistant	2023-09-21 11:22:08.548723	The correct modes and interfaces that can be protected with passwords are:\n\n1. privileged EXEC mode\n2. VTY interface\n3. console interface\n\nThese three options allow for password protection in different areas of the Cisco IOS:\n\n- Privileged EXEC mode: This mode provides access to all the commands and features of the Cisco IOS. By setting a password for privileged EXEC mode, you can restrict unauthorized access to critical configuration and management functions.\n\n- VTY interface: VTY (Virtual Terminal) interfaces are used for remote management and access to the device. By setting a password for VTY lines, you can control who can connect to the device remotely using protocols such as Telnet or SSH.\n\n- Console interface: The console interface is the physical connection to the device using a console cable. By setting a password for the console interface, you can restrict physical access to the device and prevent unauthorized configuration changes.	180	cd0327ee-4e9a-4d2c-94c6-b2eeaf459112	1
