cd934bba-7f76-442b-9b97-7ac6359b10db	user	2023-09-21 11:28:33.250169	25 What are two characteristics of RAM on a Cisco device? (Choose two.)\n25\nWhat are two characteristics of RAM on a Cisco device? (Choose two.)\n\nThe contents of RAM are lost during a power cycle.\n\nThe configuration that is actively running on the device is stored in RAM.\n\nRAM is able to store multiple versions of IOS and configuration files.\n\nRAM provides nonvolatile storage.\n\nRAM is a component in Cisco switches but not in Cisco routers.\nNavigation Bar	610	cd0327ee-4e9a-4d2c-94c6-b2eeaf459112	1
8c8e8f08-96cb-4e1a-8766-ad982d7f8915	assistant	2023-09-21 11:28:33.250269	The correct answer is:\n\n1. The contents of RAM are lost during a power cycle.\n2. The configuration that is actively running on the device is stored in RAM.\n\nRAM (Random Access Memory) on a Cisco device has the following characteristics:\n\n1. The contents of RAM are volatile, meaning they are lost when the device is powered off or restarted. This is why it is important to save the configuration to non-volatile memory, such as NVRAM or flash memory, to preserve the configuration across power cycles.\n\n2. The configuration that is actively running on the device is stored in RAM. This includes the running configuration, which is the current configuration applied to the device, as well as other temporary data and buffers used by the device.\n\nRAM is not able to store multiple versions of IOS and configuration files. Non-volatile storage, such as NVRAM or flash memory, is used for storing multiple versions of IOS and configuration files.\n\nRAM is a component in both Cisco switches and routers. It is used for temporary storage of data and configurations during device operation.	214	cd0327ee-4e9a-4d2c-94c6-b2eeaf459112	1
