cc8cebf7-99c4-4e79-a23b-5280da2ad3b8	assistant	2023-09-25 07:36:12.522409	C. Both A and B above\n\nTotal risk includes both systematic risk and unsystematic risk. \n\nSystematic risk, also known as non-diversifiable risk or market risk, is the risk that is inherent in the overall market or economy and cannot be eliminated through diversification. It is influenced by factors such as interest rates, inflation, and overall market conditions. Systematic risk affects the entire market and cannot be reduced by holding a diversified portfolio.\n\nUnsystematic risk, also known as diversifiable risk or specific risk, is the risk that is specific to a particular company or industry and can be reduced through proper diversification. It is influenced by factors such as company-specific events, management decisions, and industry-specific factors. Unsystematic risk can be reduced by holding a diversified portfolio that includes a mix of different assets or securities.\n\nTherefore, total risk includes both systematic risk and unsystematic risk, making option C the correct answer.	189	ea58514f-79a9-45dc-9198-b6f892f6d637	1
