313ccf8e-13b8-46b1-9781-857a672c05b5	assistant	2023-09-25 08:10:01.377967	To calculate the current price of the stock, we can use the dividend discount model (DDM). The DDM formula is:\n\nP = D / (rs - g)\n\nWhere:\nP = Current price of the stock\nD = Dividend expected to be received in the next period\nrs = Required rate of return on equity\ng = Growth rate of dividends\n\nIn this case, the last dividend paid (D) is $2.20, the growth rate (g) for the first year is 10%, and the growth rate (g) after the first year is 6%. The required rate of return on equity (rs) is 11%.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the dividend expected to be received in the next period:\nNext Dividend (D1) = Last Dividend (D) * (1 + g)\nNext Dividend (D1) = $2.20 * (1 + 0.10)\nNext Dividend (D1) = $2.20 * 1.10\nNext Dividend (D1) = $2.42\n\nNow, let's calculate the current price of the stock using the DDM formula:\nP = D1 / (rs - g)\nP = $2.42 / (0.11 - 0.06)\nP = $2.42 / 0.05\nP = $48.40\n\nTherefore, the current price of the stock is $48.40.\n\nThe correct answer is C. $48.40.	310	ea58514f-79a9-45dc-9198-b6f892f6d637	1
