ca07bce3-e01f-43c7-bd19-ac235fe29db4	assistant	2023-10-01 02:35:21.300395	The restart command in Docker Compose is used to specify the restart policy for a container. It can be set to one of the following options:\n\n- "no": This means that the container will not be automatically restarted if it stops or crashes.\n- "always": This means that the container will always be automatically restarted, regardless of the exit status.\n- "on-failure": This means that the container will be automatically restarted only if it stops with a non-zero exit status.\n- "unless-stopped": This means that the container will always be automatically restarted, unless it is explicitly stopped by the user.\n\nTo use the restart command in Docker Compose, you can add it under the services section of your docker-compose.yml file, like this:\n\n```\nservices:\n  myservice:\n    restart: always\n    ...\n```\n\nReplace "myservice" with the name of your service, and choose the appropriate restart policy according to your needs.	190	bba5ac11-e111-4d72-ab9a-5b34bc21b132	1
