s, phrases, and sentences in a language. It involves understanding and using words in their proper context to convey specific ideas or information.\n\n8. Pragmatics: Pragmatics refers to the social and cultural aspects of language use. It involves understanding and using language appropriately in different social situations, taking into account factors such as context, tone, and audience.\n\nUnderstanding these different parts of speech is essential for effective communication. By mastering the various components of speech, individuals can express themselves clearly, convey their intended meaning, and engage in meaningful interactions with others.	509	7d7e7f79-a23a-4ef7-805b-3bf4f0de47f1	1
