ff8492d7-369b-48a5-905d-9b9eb25f4701	assistant	2023-10-16 09:09:43.645686	To solve this problem, we can use dynamic programming. We can define a list dp of size n+1, where dp[i] represents the number of distinct ways to reach step i.\n\nSince we can only climb 1 or 2 steps at a time, the number of ways to reach step i is equal to the sum of the number of ways to reach step i-1 and the number of ways to reach step i-2.\n\nWe can initialize dp[0] = 1 and dp[1] = 1, as there is only one way to reach the first step and the second step.\n\nThen, we can iterate from step 2 to n and calculate dp[i] using the formula dp[i] = dp[i-1] + dp[i-2].\n\nFinally, the number of distinct ways to reach the top is given by dp[n].\n\nHere is the implementation in Python:\n\ndef climbStairs(n):\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1\n    dp[1] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        dp[i] = dp[i - 1] + dp[i - 2]\n    \n    return dp[n]\n\n# Example usage\nn = 3\ndistinct_ways = climbStairs(n)\nprint("Number of distinct ways to climb", n, "steps:", distinct_ways)\n\nOutput:\nNumber of distinct ways to climb 3 steps: 3\n\nSo, there are 3 distinct ways to climb 3 steps.	321	e26c2d7f-6f4a-4800-81c3-2b54328bf256	1
