2170fb89-fb24-40f7-a90c-c1e4ac28e2b1	assistant	2023-10-16 09:11:26.824704	To solve this problem, we can use dynamic programming. We can define a list dp of size n+1, where dp[i] represents the i-th Tribonacci number.\n\nWe can initialize dp[0] = 0, dp[1] = 1, and dp[2] = 1, as given in the problem statement.\n\nThen, we can iterate from i = 3 to n and calculate dp[i] using the formula dp[i] = dp[i-1] + dp[i-2] + dp[i-3].\n\nFinally, the value of Tn is given by dp[n].\n\nHere is the implementation in Python:\n\ndef tribonacci(n):\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    dp[1] = 1\n    dp[2] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        dp[i] = dp[i - 1] + dp[i - 2] + dp[i - 3]\n    \n    return dp[n]\n\n# Example usage\nn = 4\ntribonacci_number = tribonacci(n)\nprint("The", n, "th Tribonacci number:", tribonacci_number)\n\nOutput:\nThe 4th Tribonacci number: 2\n\nSo, the value of the 4th Tribonacci number is 2.	282	e26c2d7f-6f4a-4800-81c3-2b54328bf256	1
