we get:\n\n| x(1) |   | 1.5 | - (| 2.5  -4.5 |)^(-1) * | 1.75 |\n| y(1) | = | 0.5 |         (| -3     1   |)      | -2.5 |\n\nSimplifying the equation, we get:\n\n| x(1) |   | 1.5 | - (| 2.5  -4.5 |)^(-1) * | 1.75 |\n| y(1) | = | 0.5 |         (| -3     1   |)      | -2.5 |\n\n| x(1) |   | 1.5 | - (| a  b |) * | 1.75 |\n| y(1) | = | 0.5 |         (| c  d |)      | -2.5 |\n\nSolving the equation, we can find the updated approximations x(1) and y(1). Repeat this process until the desired level of accuracy is achieved.\n\nNote: The actual values of a, b, c, and d in the inverse of the Jacobian matrix need to be calculated using matrix algebra or software tools.	967	c6b08a86-bacf-4c96-be5a-26664b7aec05	1
