an `onClick` event listener to trigger the conversion when the button is clicked.\n\n```jsx\nfunction ConversionButton({ onClick }) {\n  return (\n    <button onClick={onClick}>Convert</button>\n  );\n}\n\n// In your main app component:\n<ConversionButton onClick={handleConversion} />\n```\n\n5. Display the converted temperature:\n   - In your output field component, display the converted temperature value from the state variable.\n\n```jsx\nfunction OutputField({ convertedTemperature }) {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Converted Temperature: {convertedTemperature}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\n// In your main app component:\n<OutputField convertedTemperature={convertedTemperature} />\n```\n\nBy following these steps, you should be able to implement the conversion logic in your temperature converter app. Adjust the conversion formula and temperature scales according to your specific requirements.	542	d1d22482-ef2d-44fa-abac-992e5381a2af	1
