k extends RecursiveTask<Integer> {\n    protected Integer compute() {\n        // Code to be executed in the thread\n    }\n}\n\nForkJoinPool forkJoinPool = new ForkJoinPool();\nMyRecursiveTask task = new MyRecursiveTask();\nint result = forkJoinPool.invoke(task);\n```\n\nThese are the main ways to create and manage threads in Java. Each approach has its own advantages and use cases, so choose the one that best fits your requirements.	493	621782c4-3aef-41b0-9854-ae4dbc08ba0b	1
