fied character encoding.\n   - It provides methods like write(int) and write(char[]) to write characters to the underlying byte stream.\n   - OutputStreamWriter is commonly used when you need to write text to a byte stream, such as writing text to a file using FileOutputStream.\n\nIn summary, character streams are used for reading and writing text-based data, while byte streams are used for reading and writing binary data. InputStreamReader is used to convert byte streams into character streams, and OutputStreamWriter is used to convert character streams into byte streams. These classes provide a convenient way to work with different types of data and handle the conversion between bytes and characters.	483	3a5d7e58-484d-4f20-8ed9-2bd24f16041d	1
