31f9fe64-2dbc-4896-bacb-f41470a9aeb4	assistant	2023-11-11 15:28:26.983122	The formula for the sum of the squares of the first n natural numbers can be represented using sigma notation as:\n\nΣi^2 = 1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + ... + n^2\n\nTo calculate this sum, you can use the formula:\n\nΣi^2 = (n * (n + 1) * (2n + 1)) / 6\n\nThis formula is derived from the sum of squares formula:\n\nΣi^2 = (n * (n + 1) * (2n + 1)) / 6\n\nFor example, if you want to find the sum of the squares of the first 5 natural numbers, you can substitute n = 5 into the formula:\n\nΣi^2 = (5 * (5 + 1) * (2 * 5 + 1)) / 6\n      = (5 * 6 * 11) / 6\n      = 55\n\nSo, the sum of the squares of the first 5 natural numbers is 55.	224	0050ea4e-b26c-4370-a529-94340ab399ff	1
