58b4f79f-ae73-410f-b6a6-51e8ff337cc8	assistant	2023-11-11 15:27:04.644773	Sigma notation, also known as summation notation, is a mathematical notation used to represent the sum of a series of terms. It is denoted by the Greek letter sigma (Σ). Here are a few examples of sigma notation:\n\n1. Example: Sum of the first n natural numbers\n   The sum of the first n natural numbers can be represented using sigma notation as:\n   Σi = 1 + 2 + 3 + ... + n\n\n2. Example: Sum of the squares of the first n natural numbers\n   The sum of the squares of the first n natural numbers can be represented using sigma notation as:\n   Σi^2 = 1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + ... + n^2\n\n3. Example: Sum of the even numbers from 2 to 10\n   The sum of the even numbers from 2 to 10 can be represented using sigma notation as:\n   Σ2i = 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 + 10\n\n4. Example: Sum of the reciprocals of the first n natural numbers\n   The sum of the reciprocals of the first n natural numbers can be represented using sigma notation as:\n   Σ1/i = 1/1 + 1/2 + 1/3 + ... + 1/n\n\nThese are just a few examples of sigma notation. It is a powerful tool for representing and calculating sums of series in a concise and compact manner.	310	0050ea4e-b26c-4370-a529-94340ab399ff	1
