reted and applied in a manner that promotes equality and addresses historical injustices.\n\nTo avoid a potential violation of Section 9(3), the courts and lawmakers should interpret and apply Section 27 of the Insolvency Act in a manner that takes into account the transformative goals of the Constitution. This may involve considering alternative measures or safeguards to ensure that the sequestration process does not unfairly discriminate against individuals or groups who are already marginalized or disadvantaged.\n\nOverall, the potential violation of Section 9(3) by Section 27 of the Insolvency Act highlights the need for a transformative approach to constitutional interpretation and the importance of promoting equality and addressing historical injustices in the application of laws and policies.	499	1c214d39-b235-4090-9190-fd9843624c68	1
