opment experiences, perceptions, and challenges.\n   - Coding: Use coding techniques to categorize and organize the qualitative data, allowing for the identification of key themes and sub-themes.\n\n2. Quantitative Analysis:\n   - Descriptive statistics: Analyze the survey data using descriptive statistics to summarize the participants' responses and provide an overview of their professional development practices, perceptions, and preferences.\n   - Inferential statistics: Conduct inferential statistical analysis, such as correlation or regression analysis, to examine relationships between variables, such as the impact of professional development on teaching practices or student learning outcomes.\n\nIntegration of Findings:\nThe qualitative and quantitative findings will be integrated to provide a comprehensive understanding of ELT teachers' professional development experiences. The qualitative data will provide rich, in-depth insights, while the quantitative data will provide a broader perspective and allow for generalizations.\n\nEthical Considerations:\n- Obtain informed consent from participants before conducting interviews, focus groups, or surveys.\n- Ensure confidentiality and anonymity of participants by assigning pseudonyms and securely storing data.\n- Adhere to ethical guidelines and obtain necessary ethical approvals from relevant institutions.\n\nBy employing a mixed-methods approach, this research design and methodology will provide a holistic understanding of ELT teachers' professional development experiences, perceptions, and preferences. It will allow for a comprehensive analysis of the factors that influence professional development and inform future directions for ELT teachers' professional development programs.	617	6069f3e4-4f90-48d7-9d94-8102b5bfc8a8	1
