a4536a3d-6e64-4f64-86b9-ca135ce07293	user	2023-10-27 07:19:52.050972	9 What is the function of STP in a scalable network?\n9\nWhat is the function of STP in a scalable network?\n\nIt protects the edge of the enterprise network from malicious activity.\n\nIt combines multiple switch trunk links to act as one logical link for increased bandwidth.\n\nIt decreases the size of the failure domain to contain the impact of failures.\n\nIt disables redundant paths to eliminate Layer 2 loops.\nNavigation Bar	891	eeb0bdd6-0ef8-4fd1-8de7-64ee014b8e3c	1
21a79313-00d5-486c-bb78-0e7d5c13acea	assistant	2023-10-27 07:19:52.051078	The correct answer is: It disables redundant paths to eliminate Layer 2 loops.\n\nThe main function of Spanning Tree Protocol (STP) in a scalable network is to prevent and eliminate Layer 2 loops. Layer 2 loops can occur when there are redundant paths in the network, which can lead to broadcast storms, MAC address table instability, and network congestion. STP works by identifying and disabling redundant paths, ensuring that there is only one active path between any two network devices. This helps to create a loop-free topology and ensures that data is forwarded along the most efficient path, preventing network disruptions and improving network stability.	125	eeb0bdd6-0ef8-4fd1-8de7-64ee014b8e3c	1
