94c4fb09-5b4c-40c5-b6de-3739013f4b47	assistant	2023-10-27 07:04:58.04693	The correct answer is: Frames are forwarded without any error checking.\n\nCut-through switching is a switching method where frames are forwarded as soon as the destination MAC address is read, without waiting for the entire frame to be received. In cut-through switching, the switch only reads the destination MAC address and immediately starts forwarding the frame. This means that frames are forwarded without any error checking, as the switch does not wait for the entire frame to be received and checked for errors. This results in lower latency but does not provide error detection or correction.	107	eeb0bdd6-0ef8-4fd1-8de7-64ee014b8e3c	1
