8284885a-83f4-47a8-a37d-bfdaef2526f8	assistant	2023-10-27 07:20:37.161894	The two drawbacks to turning spanning tree off and having multiple paths through the Layer 2 switch network are:\n\n1. Broadcast frames are transmitted indefinitely: Without spanning tree, there is no mechanism to prevent broadcast storms caused by loops in the network. Broadcast frames can be continuously forwarded in a loop, leading to network congestion and performance issues.\n\n2. The MAC address table becomes unstable: Without spanning tree, there is a higher likelihood of MAC address table instability. This can occur when multiple paths exist between switches, causing the MAC address table to constantly update and potentially leading to incorrect forwarding of frames.\n\nThe other options mentioned, such as port security shutting down ports or the switch acting like a hub, are not directly related to the drawbacks of turning off spanning tree and having multiple paths in the Layer 2 switch network.	161	eeb0bdd6-0ef8-4fd1-8de7-64ee014b8e3c	1
