db8ffb38-d7e9-43d4-a79d-4423ee839602	assistant	2023-10-27 07:33:13.532097	The correct order of DHCP message types in the DHCPv4 process is as follows:\n\n1. DHCPDISCOVER: The client sends a broadcast message to discover available DHCP servers on the network.\n\n2. DHCPOFFER: The DHCP server responds with a unicast message offering IP address lease and other configuration parameters to the client.\n\n3. DHCPREQUEST: The client selects one of the offered IP addresses and sends a broadcast message requesting that IP address from the DHCP server.\n\n4. DHCPACK: The DHCP server acknowledges the client's request by sending a unicast message confirming the lease of the requested IP address.\n\nNote: DHCPREPLY and DHCPINFORMATION-REQUEST are not part of the DHCPv4 process.	144	eeb0bdd6-0ef8-4fd1-8de7-64ee014b8e3c	1
