06878e1d-0b38-4ed5-a295-1f2f5165b649	assistant	2023-10-27 07:56:00.444752	The correct answer is:\n\nEnable BPDU guard.\n\nDisable DTP.\n\nUse private VLANs.\n\nThese are three techniques for mitigating VLAN attacks:\n\n1. Enable BPDU guard: BPDU (Bridge Protocol Data Unit) guard is a feature that can be enabled on switch ports to protect against unauthorized switches being connected to the network. When BPDU guard is enabled, if a switch receives a BPDU on a port that is not configured as a trunk port, the port will be put into an error-disabled state, preventing any further communication.\n\n2. Disable DTP: DTP (Dynamic Trunking Protocol) is a Cisco proprietary protocol that is used to negotiate trunk links between switches. However, it can also be exploited by attackers to gain unauthorized access to VLANs. By disabling DTP on switch ports, the risk of VLAN hopping attacks can be mitigated.\n\n3. Use private VLANs: Private VLANs (PVLANs) are a feature that allows for further segmentation and isolation within a VLAN. PVLANs can be used to restrict communication between devices within the same VLAN, preventing attacks such as VLAN hopping. By configuring ports to be part of different PVLANs, communication between devices can be limited to specific ports or VLANs, enhancing network security.	255	eeb0bdd6-0ef8-4fd1-8de7-64ee014b8e3c	1
