b3fb143d-0cb6-45b0-b434-cc72f36e3e28	assistant	2023-10-27 07:58:35.595569	The correct answer is:\n\nIt checks the source MAC address in the Ethernet header against the sender MAC address in the ARP body.\n\nThe command "ip arp inspection validate src-mac" is used to configure Dynamic ARP Inspection (DAI) on a switch. DAI is a security feature that helps prevent ARP spoofing attacks by validating the source MAC address in the Ethernet header against the sender MAC address in the ARP body. If the MAC addresses do not match, the ARP packet is dropped, indicating a potential ARP spoofing attempt. This helps protect the network from malicious ARP attacks.	116	eeb0bdd6-0ef8-4fd1-8de7-64ee014b8e3c	1
