 it beneficial. Positive perceptions of professional development can lead to increased motivation, active participation, and a willingness to implement new strategies in the classroom.\n\nIn summary, efficacy, attitude, beliefs, and perceptions all play important roles in ELT teachers' professional development. Teachers with high efficacy, positive attitudes, growth-oriented beliefs, and favorable perceptions of professional development are more likely to actively engage in continuous learning, seek out development opportunities, and implement new strategies in their teaching practice.	411	95d76acc-7f28-4c54-ac24-3e71ec22a39a	1
