nance, corruption, and inadequate institutional capacity can hinder sustainable development efforts. Effective governance structures, transparency, accountability, and the rule of law are essential for implementing and monitoring sustainable development policies and initiatives.\n\n7. Population growth and urbanization: Rapid population growth and urbanization pose challenges to sustainable development. They put pressure on resources, infrastructure, and services, leading to increased energy consumption, waste generation, and environmental degradation. Managing urbanization and promoting sustainable urban development are crucial for achieving sustainable development goals.\n\nAddressing these core problems requires a comprehensive and integrated approach that involves governments, businesses, civil society, and individuals. It involves promoting sustainable consumption and production patterns, investing in renewable energy and clean technologies, promoting social inclusion and equity, protecting ecosystems and biodiversity, and strengthening governance and institutional capacity.	473	10496a1d-8b47-4eeb-8f78-1a245033514a	1
