370941cd-d025-4670-a280-56e0835ccc1f	assistant	2023-11-12 18:13:52.649307	To factorize the expression x^4 - 4x^3 - x^2 + 4x, we can use factoring by grouping. Here are the steps:\n\nStep 1: Group the terms in pairs:\n(x^4 - 4x^3) - (x^2 - 4x)\n\nStep 2: Factor out the greatest common factor from each pair:\nx^3(x - 4) - x(x - 4)\n\nStep 3: Notice that we now have a common binomial factor, (x - 4). Factor it out:\n(x - 4)(x^3 - x)\n\nStep 4: The expression x^3 - x can be further factored by factoring out the greatest common factor, which is x:\n(x - 4)x(x^2 - 1)\n\nStep 5: The expression x^2 - 1 is a difference of squares and can be factored as:\n(x - 4)x(x - 1)(x + 1)\n\nTherefore, the factored form of x^4 - 4x^3 - x^2 + 4x is (x - 4)x(x - 1)(x + 1).	252	5322247f-b3db-4105-bdba-87bb9d882706	1
