                 for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {\n                     cout << arr[i][j][k] << " ";\n                 }\n             }\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - Nested Loops: Three nested loops where each loop iterates over the entire input.\n     ```cpp\n     void nestedLoops(int n) {\n         for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n             for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                 for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {\n                     // Perform some operation\n                 }\n             }\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n\nThese examples demonstrate the time complexity of different algorithms in C++. It's important to note that the actual running time of an algorithm can vary based on various factors, such as hardware, compiler optimizations, and input data. Time complexity analysis provides an understanding of how the algorithm's performance scales with the input size.	713	e67dc9bf-8e8d-48cc-bfb2-d3f06f94ce1f	1
