baf84461-87e9-4f8a-b842-b00e8913ef4b	assistant	2023-11-15 14:25:13.571491	Background:\nEnglish Language Teaching (ELT) plays a crucial role in equipping students with the necessary language skills for communication and academic success. Effective ELT instruction requires well-trained and continuously developing teachers. Professional development programs aim to enhance teachers' knowledge, skills, and pedagogical practices. However, the effectiveness and impact of professional development for ELT secondary school teachers are influenced by various factors, including the current practices, perceptions, and challenges faced by teachers in their professional development.\n\nStatement of the Problem:\nDespite the recognized importance of professional development for ELT secondary school teachers, there is a need to examine the current practices, perceptions, and challenges in order to improve the effectiveness and impact of professional development programs. The problem statement for this research is as follows:\n\n1. Current Practices: What are the existing practices of professional development for ELT secondary school teachers? How frequently do teachers engage in professional development activities? What are the main types of professional development programs offered to ELT secondary school teachers?\n\n2. Perceptions: What are the attitudes, beliefs, and motivations of ELT secondary school teachers towards professional development? What do teachers perceive as the benefits and challenges of engaging in professional development? How do teachers' perceptions influence their participation and engagement in professional development activities?\n\n3. Challenges: What are the common challenges faced by ELT secondary school teachers in their professional development? What external factors, such as time constraints and lack of resources, hinder teachers' engagement in professional development? What internal factors, such as teacher beliefs and self-efficacy, affect teachers' willingness to participate in professional development activities?\n\nBy addressing these research questions, this study aims to provide insights into the current practices, perceptions, and challenges of professional development for ELT secondary school teachers. The findings will contribute to the improvement of professional development programs and practices, ultimately enhancing the quality of ELT instruction in secondary schools.	377	3a71cd8e-ce02-4f90-bb5b-a3eea1d062fb	1
