d218e0b8-a755-4af4-913f-91d1d52a5b25	assistant	2023-11-15 06:42:05.64468	1. Demand and want are similar in that they both refer to a desire for something. However, there is a slight difference between the two. Want refers to a general desire or wish for something, whereas demand refers to a want backed by purchasing power. In other words, demand is the willingness and ability to pay for a desired good or service.\n\n2. We cannot purchase all that we need or desire to have due to various factors such as limited resources, budget constraints, and availability. Our needs and desires are often greater than what is realistically attainable. Additionally, individual preferences and priorities also play a role in determining what we choose to purchase.\n\n3. Generally, a decrease in the price of a commodity leads to an increase in the quantity demanded by consumers. This is known as the law of demand. When the price of a product decreases, it becomes relatively cheaper compared to other goods, making it more attractive to consumers. As a result, consumers are more likely to buy more of the product.\n\n4. Demand curves slope downwards from left to right due to the law of demand. The law of demand states that as the price of a product increases, the quantity demanded decreases, and vice versa. This is because as the price of a product increases, consumers are less willing or able to purchase it. On the other hand, as the price decreases, consumers are more willing and able to buy more of the product.\n\nExceptions to the downward-sloping demand curve can occur in certain situations. For example, Veblen goods are luxury goods that defy the law of demand. As the price of Veblen goods increases, their demand may also increase due to their perceived status or exclusivity. Additionally, Giffen goods are another exception where the demand for a product increases as its price increases, typically due to income constraints and substitution effects. However, these exceptions are relatively rare and do not apply to most goods and services.	388	ea37ddd8-f371-41e7-84d9-2ec97b69c989	1
