chers in their professional development.\n   - Discussion of external factors such as time constraints, lack of resources, and institutional support.\n   - Examination of internal factors such as teacher beliefs, motivation, and self-efficacy in relation to professional development.\n   - Exploration of strategies and recommendations for overcoming these challenges.\n\n5. Gaps and Future Directions:\n   - Identification of gaps in the existing literature on ELT professional development for secondary school teachers.\n   - Discussion of areas for further research and exploration.\n   - Suggestions for improving professional development programs and practices for ELT secondary school teachers.\n\nIt is important to conduct a comprehensive search of relevant databases, journals, and other sources to gather a wide range of literature for the review. The literature review should critically analyze and synthesize the findings from different studies, highlighting the key themes, trends, and gaps in the existing research.	482	3a71cd8e-ce02-4f90-bb5b-a3eea1d062fb	1
