3a6d882d-31ad-4bcc-aeb7-44446897f2d1	assistant	2023-11-16 10:02:40.740356	When it comes to quoting style for your PhD research on ELT teachers' professional development, there are several commonly used styles that you can consider. The choice of style depends on the requirements of your institution or the guidelines provided by your supervisor. Here are three popular citation styles that are often used in academic research:\n\n1. APA (American Psychological Association) Style: This style is widely used in the social sciences, including education. It provides clear guidelines for citing sources in-text and in the reference list. APA style emphasizes the author-date format for in-text citations and includes a comprehensive reference list at the end of the document.\n\n2. MLA (Modern Language Association) Style: MLA style is commonly used in the humanities, including language and literature studies. It focuses on providing concise in-text citations and a detailed works cited page. MLA style uses the author-page format for in-text citations.\n\n3. Chicago Manual of Style: The Chicago style is often used in history, social sciences, and some humanities disciplines. It offers two different citation systems: the notes and bibliography system and the author-date system. The notes and bibliography system uses footnotes or endnotes for in-text citations, while the author-date system uses parenthetical citations.\n\nIt is important to consult the specific guidelines provided by your institution or supervisor to determine which citation style is preferred for your research. Additionally, using reference management software such as EndNote, Zotero, or Mendeley can help you easily manage and format your citations according to the chosen style.	303	980a2202-f435-4b74-9178-624fd7a078ac	1
