develop their knowledge and skills over time.\n\n6. Collaboration and Networking: Professional development programs should encourage collaboration and networking among ELT secondary school teachers. This can involve creating communities of practice, facilitating peer observation and feedback, and providing opportunities for teachers to share their experiences and expertise.\n\n7. Evaluation and Reflection: Professional development programs should include mechanisms for evaluation and reflection. Teachers should have opportunities to assess the impact of their professional development activities on their teaching practice and student learning outcomes. This feedback can inform future professional development initiatives.\n\nWhile these principles and guidelines are not internationally standardized, they provide a framework for designing and implementing effective professional development programs for ELT secondary school teachers. It is important for educational institutions and policymakers to consider these principles and adapt them to their specific contexts and needs.	470	3a71cd8e-ce02-4f90-bb5b-a3eea1d062fb	1
