16e953ca-0b75-4d79-aa0f-bfa505a27389	assistant	2023-11-16 07:23:23.488807	Professional Skills:\n1. Pedagogical Skills: ELT secondary school teachers need to have strong pedagogical skills, including lesson planning, classroom management, and assessment techniques.\n2. Communication Skills: Effective communication skills are essential for ELT teachers to convey information clearly, facilitate classroom discussions, and provide feedback to students.\n3. Technology Skills: In today's digital age, ELT teachers should be proficient in using technology tools and resources to enhance their teaching and engage students in meaningful learning experiences.\n4. Adaptability: ELT teachers should be adaptable and flexible in their teaching approaches to meet the diverse needs and learning styles of their students.\n5. Collaboration: Collaborative skills are important for ELT teachers to work effectively with colleagues, administrators, and other stakeholders in the education community.\n\nEthics:\n1. Professionalism: ELT teachers should demonstrate professionalism by maintaining confidentiality, being punctual, and adhering to ethical guidelines and standards in their teaching practice.\n2. Respect: ELT teachers should treat their students, colleagues, and other members of the school community with respect, valuing diversity and promoting inclusivity.\n3. Integrity: ELT teachers should act with integrity, being honest, fair, and transparent in their interactions with students, parents, and colleagues.\n4. Confidentiality: ELT teachers should respect the privacy and confidentiality of their students, ensuring that personal information is handled appropriately and securely.\n\nKnowledge:\n1. Language Proficiency: ELT secondary school teachers should have a strong command of the English language, including grammar, vocabulary, and pronunciation.\n2. Content Knowledge: They should have a deep understanding of the subject matter they are teaching, including language skills, literature, and cultural aspects of English-speaking countries.\n3. Pedagogical Knowledge: ELT teachers should be knowledgeable about effective teaching methodologies, theories of language acquisition, and assessment practices.\n4. Cultural Awareness: ELT teachers should have an understanding of different cultures and be sensitive to the cultural backgrounds and needs of their students.\n\nRelations:\n1. Student-Teacher Relationships: ELT teachers should build positive and supportive relationships with their students, creating a safe and inclusive learning environment.\n2. Parent-Teacher Relationships: ELT teachers should establish open and effective communication with parents, involving them in their child's education and providing regular updates on their progress.\n3. Colleague Relationships: ELT teachers should collaborate and share ideas with their colleagues, fostering a supportive and professional learning community.\n4. Professional Networks: ELT teachers should actively engage in professional networks and associations, attending conferences, workshops, and seminars to connect with other professionals in the field and stay updated with the latest research and practices.\n\nIn summary, ELT secondary school teachers need to possess professional skills such as pedagogical and communication skills, adhere to ethical guidelines, have a strong knowledge base in language, content, and pedagogy, and build positive relationships with students, parents, colleagues, and professional networks. These attributes contribute to their professional development and effectiveness as ELT teachers.	604	95d76acc-7f28-4c54-ac24-3e71ec22a39a	1
