building professional networks, participating in communities of practice, and engaging in collaborative learning opportunities. Collaboration and networking provide opportunities for ELT teachers to exchange knowledge, receive feedback, and expand their professional horizons.\n\n4. Integration of technology: Both practices and trends in ELT teachers' professional development recognize the increasing role of technology in language teaching and learning. Practices such as attending workshops or webinars on integrating technology into the classroom, exploring online resources and tools, or participating in online courses or communities focused on technology-enhanced language teaching are common among ELT teachers. Trends in professional development also often emphasize the integration of technology as a means to enhance teaching and learning outcomes. This includes trends such as blended learning, flipped classrooms, and the use of digital tools and platforms for assessment and feedback.\n\nIn summary, practices and trends in ELT teachers' professional development share similarities in their focus on improvement, emphasis on reflective practice, promotion of collaboration and networking, and integration of technology. Understanding and engaging with both practices and trends can support ELT teachers in their ongoing growth and development as professionals.	527	feb218aa-9773-49bb-bdb8-83722a1dc6cd	1
