 revisions to improve the clarity and coherence of your paraphrased text.\n\n9. Cite the Original Source: Even when paraphrasing, it is important to provide proper citations to acknowledge the original source. Include an in-text citation and a reference in the appropriate citation style.\n\n10. Seek Feedback: Share your paraphrased text with peers, advisors, or colleagues to get feedback on its clarity, accuracy, and originality. Incorporate their suggestions to further refine your paraphrasing skills.\n\nRemember, paraphrasing is not about simply replacing words or rearranging sentences. It involves understanding the original text, capturing the main ideas, and expressing them in your own words while maintaining accuracy and integrity. By practicing these strategies, you can effectively paraphrase your PhD research proposal on ELT teachers' professional development.	517	daa217ee-9fbe-4877-8210-f0dbc7a9b3a9	1
