e and implement evidence-based strategies to improve student outcomes.\n\n7. Professional Learning Communities (PLCs): PLCs are groups of teachers who collaborate regularly to improve their teaching practices. PLCs provide a supportive environment for teachers to share experiences, discuss challenges, and develop solutions collectively.\n\n8. Mentoring and Coaching: Mentoring and coaching programs are becoming more prevalent in professional development. Experienced teachers or instructional coaches provide guidance, support, and feedback to less experienced teachers, helping them develop their teaching skills.\n\n9. International Conferences and Exchanges: Teachers may have opportunities to attend international conferences or participate in teacher exchange programs. These experiences expose teachers to different teaching methodologies, cultural perspectives, and global trends in ELT.\n\nIt is important to note that the specific practices and trends may vary depending on the context, resources, and policies in Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, and other parts of Africa.	501	ba3cd63f-e721-464a-b974-2823a7153e28	1
