ay to confirm that it is sorted.\n   - Average-case scenario: The average-case time complexity of Insertion Sort is O(n^2). This is because, on average, it will need to make n/2 passes through the array, and each pass requires shifting elements to make room for the current element being inserted.\n   - Worst-case scenario: The worst-case time complexity of Insertion Sort is O(n^2). This occurs when the array is sorted in reverse order, and Insertion Sort needs to make n passes through the array, each time shifting elements to make room for the current element being inserted.\n\nIn terms of space complexity, all three algorithms have a space complexity of O(1) since they only require a constant amount of additional space to store temporary variables.\n\nIt's important to note that while Bubble Sort, Selection Sort, and Insertion Sort are simple and easy to understand, they are not the most efficient sorting algorithms for large datasets. There are other sorting algorithms, such as Merge Sort or Quick Sort, that have better average and worst-case time complexities.	622	b253e283-6e30-4935-9816-9fba0adb7dc9	1
