cf542add-bab2-4416-afe2-c6e8a430aca7	assistant	2023-11-17 18:33:16.105988	ኅብር (həbr) and ህብረት (həbrət) are both Amharic words, but they have slightly different meanings.\n\nኅብር (həbr) refers to "knowledge" or "wisdom." It represents the understanding and awareness that one gains through learning, education, and experience. It can also refer to the accumulation of knowledge in a particular field or subject.\n\nህብረት (həbrət), on the other hand, refers to "education" or "learning." It represents the process of acquiring knowledge, skills, and values through formal or informal means. It encompasses the activities, methods, and institutions involved in imparting knowledge and facilitating learning.\n\nIn summary, ኅብር (həbr) refers to the actual knowledge or wisdom, while ህብረት (həbrət) refers to the process of acquiring that knowledge through education and learning.	232	8b624ecd-dd5e-4b5e-ab94-2c3e8dc9a7b0	1
