dcc069b2-f537-4751-a6e4-321523e83b61	assistant	2023-11-18 19:11:46.684309	In your PhD proposal and research, you can develop a conceptual and theoretical framework that explores the relationship between perception, attitude, beliefs, and efficacy of ELT teachers in professional development. \n\nThe general term that encompasses all these factors is "perception." Perception refers to how ELT teachers perceive professional development, including their attitudes, beliefs, and efficacy. It serves as the overarching concept that connects these different elements together.\n\nTo develop your conceptual framework, you can start by defining and explaining each of these factors in relation to professional development. For example:\n\n1. Perception: This refers to how ELT teachers perceive professional development, including their overall attitude, beliefs, and efficacy in engaging with and benefiting from professional development opportunities.\n\n2. Attitude: This encompasses the teacher's disposition and feelings towards professional development. It includes their willingness to engage, openness to new ideas, and motivation to improve their teaching skills through professional development.\n\n3. Beliefs: These are the deeply held convictions and assumptions that teachers have about teaching and learning. They shape their instructional practices and influence their decision-making processes. In the context of professional development, teachers' beliefs can impact their willingness to adopt new strategies or approaches.\n\n4. Efficacy: This refers to teachers' confidence in their ability to successfully implement new knowledge and skills acquired through professional development. It is closely linked to self-efficacy, which is the belief in one's own capabilities to achieve specific goals. Teachers with high efficacy are more likely to take risks, experiment with new strategies, and persist in the face of challenges.\n\nOnce you have defined these factors, you can then explore the theoretical underpinnings and existing research that supports the relationship between perception, attitude, beliefs, and efficacy in ELT teachers' professional development. This may involve reviewing relevant literature, theories, and models that have been used to study these factors in the context of professional development.\n\nBy developing a conceptual and theoretical framework that integrates perception, attitude, beliefs, and efficacy, you can provide a comprehensive understanding of how these factors interact and influence ELT teachers' engagement and outcomes in professional development. This framework will guide your research design, data collection, and analysis, helping you to explore the research questions and hypotheses in your PhD proposal.	449	7d97ed3e-fcaa-4760-a064-2c2b9c0bce5a	1
