 software. Calculate descriptive statistics (e.g., mean, standard deviation) to understand the overall teacher efficacy levels. You can also conduct inferential statistics (e.g., t-tests, ANOVA) to explore potential relationships between teacher efficacy and other variables of interest.\n\n7. Interpretation: Interpret the findings based on the data analysis. Examine the teachers' efficacy levels, identify any patterns or differences, and relate them to the current practices, perceptions, and challenges of EFL/ELT professional development in government secondary schools in Addis Ababa.\n\n8. Reporting: Present your findings in a clear and organized manner, using tables, charts, and narratives. Discuss the implications of the teacher efficacy levels for EFL/ELT professional development and make recommendations for improving practices in government secondary schools.\n\nRemember to obtain ethical approval for your research and ensure the confidentiality and anonymity of the participants throughout the process.	558	6307de4a-ad7b-42c1-b723-790e828ee010	1
