ation, cooking skills training, and promoting awareness of the economic benefits of healthy eating.\n\n6. Policy and advocacy: Economic interventions often involve advocating for policies that support nutrition and health. This may include working with policymakers to develop and implement strategies that address food insecurity, improve food environments, and reduce inequalities in access to nutritious foods.\n\nThe economic approach to nutrition interventions recognizes that addressing economic barriers and incentives is crucial for improving nutrition outcomes. By considering the economic factors that influence food choices and access to nutritious foods, interventions can be designed to create an environment that supports healthier eating habits and improves overall nutrition status.	418	3d0ab6f4-7cf4-4e3d-9617-29d6d3ad0f4b	1
