1b42aed4-a61e-4f79-ae9f-7418efa27c23	assistant	2023-12-12 20:57:14.145455	To determine when students A and B will be side by side for the first time, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their individual times to complete one round.\n\nStudent A takes 6 minutes to complete one round, and student B takes 14 minutes. To find the LCM of 6 and 14, we can list the multiples of each number until we find a common multiple:\n\nMultiples of 6: 6, 12, 18, 24, 30, 36, 42, 48, 54, 60, ...\n\nMultiples of 14: 14, 28, 42, 56, 70, 84, 98, ...\n\nFrom the lists above, we can see that the least common multiple of 6 and 14 is 42.\n\nTherefore, student A and student B will be side by side for the first time after 42 minutes.	193	11f7490b-99c9-4576-89c6-46469567abcc	1
