s of technology. Software engineering skills can be utilized to develop software applications that address societal challenges, such as privacy concerns, algorithmic bias, or digital divide.\n\nThese are just a few examples of how social science and software engineering can intersect. By combining knowledge and skills from both fields, researchers and practitioners can gain a deeper understanding of the social aspects of technology and develop innovative solutions.	375	0cdc3096-56cb-4a37-b459-827299c2df5b	1
