5ad9295e-40b9-40b7-bac6-2a4dddeefc6c	assistant	2023-12-12 04:43:41.819257	Sure! Selection sort is another simple sorting algorithm that works by repeatedly finding the minimum element from the unsorted part of the array and putting it at the beginning. This process is repeated until the entire array is sorted.\n\nHere's an example of how you can implement selection sort in Python:\n\n```python\ndef selection_sort(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    \n    # Traverse through all array elements\n    for i in range(n):\n        \n        # Find the minimum element in the unsorted part of the array\n        min_idx = i\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if arr[j] < arr[min_idx]:\n                min_idx = j\n        \n        # Swap the found minimum element with the first element\n        arr[i], arr[min_idx] = arr[min_idx], arr[i]\n    \n    return arr\n\n# Example usage\nmy_list = [64, 34, 25, 12, 22, 11, 90]\nsorted_list = selection_sort(my_list)\nprint(sorted_list)\n```\n\nThis will output: `[11, 12, 22, 25, 34, 64, 90]`\n\nIn this example, we define a function `selection_sort` that takes an array as input. We use two nested loops to iterate through the array and find the minimum element in the unsorted part. We then swap the minimum element with the first element of the unsorted part. This process is repeated until the entire array is sorted.\n\nLet me know if you need any further assistance!	314	99c42813-15c4-486b-a7eb-7776ab5806ca	1
