ed time to avoid rushing or leaving questions unanswered.\n\n9. Review your answers: After completing the section, review your answers and check for any errors or overlooked details. Make sure your answers are logical and supported by evidence from the passage.\n\n10. Practice regularly: Regular practice is key to improving your skills in SAT English. Use official SAT practice materials, online resources, and practice tests to familiarize yourself with the question types and develop your analytical and logical thinking abilities.\n\nRemember, consistent practice and a thorough understanding of grammar rules and reading strategies will help you excel in SAT English analytical and logical questions.	469	1e326e6a-7ce7-4db4-ac63-87f1f230f2be	1
