457dec59-9200-407d-871d-a5cb14b510bc	assistant	2023-12-02 12:17:40.910816	Bed making is an essential skill in nursing that involves creating a clean, comfortable, and safe environment for patients. Here are the steps to follow when making a bed in a healthcare setting:\n\n1. Gather the necessary supplies: You will need clean linens, including a fitted sheet, flat sheet, pillowcase(s), and any additional items like blankets or bed pads.\n\n2. Prepare the bed: Start by ensuring the bed is at a comfortable height for you to work. Lower the side rails if necessary and lock the wheels to prevent the bed from moving.\n\n3. Remove the soiled linens: If the bed is occupied, assist the patient in turning onto their side while supporting their back. Remove the soiled linens, rolling them inward to contain any dirt or debris. Place them in a designated laundry bag or hamper.\n\n4. Clean the mattress: Inspect the mattress for any stains or spills. If necessary, clean the mattress using appropriate cleaning solutions and allow it to dry before proceeding.\n\n5. Apply a mattress protector or bed pad: If needed, place a waterproof mattress protector or bed pad on the mattress to protect it from any potential spills or accidents.\n\n6. Fit the bottom sheet: Start by placing the fitted sheet on the mattress, ensuring it is centered and taut. Smooth out any wrinkles or creases, tucking the corners securely under the mattress.\n\n7. Add the top sheet: Place the flat sheet over the fitted sheet, ensuring it is centered and the top edge aligns with the top of the mattress. Tuck the bottom edge of the sheet under the mattress, leaving enough length to fold it back over the blanket or comforter.\n\n8. Arrange the blanket or comforter: If needed, place a blanket or comforter on top of the sheet, ensuring it is centered and covers the entire bed. Fold the top edge of the sheet and blanket or comforter back over the bed, creating a neat and finished appearance.\n\n9. Position the pillows: Place the pillows in their appropriate positions, ensuring they are clean and fluffed. Add pillowcases to each pillow, tucking the open end of the pillowcase under the pillow to secure it.\n\n10. Adjust the bed height and side rails: If necessary, adjust the bed height to the patient's preference and safety. Ensure the side rails are raised and locked, if needed, to prevent falls.\n\n11. Dispose of any waste and clean the surrounding area: Remove any waste or soiled linens from the room and dispose of them properly. Clean and sanitize the surrounding area, ensuring a clean and hygienic environment for the patient.\n\nRemember to follow infection control protocols, including proper hand hygiene and the use of personal protective equipment (PPE) when necessary. Regularly change and launder linens to maintain cleanliness and prevent the spread of infections.	570	3d3527e9-d101-4243-a1b3-6ec0bdf53e24	1
