d13ebe83-51b4-48c3-b995-383b8e2ef0d3	assistant	2023-12-03 10:00:05.509141	The main difference between a teller and a banker is their level of responsibility and the scope of their job duties.\n\nA teller primarily focuses on handling customer transactions at the front counter of a bank. They are responsible for processing deposits, withdrawals, and other basic transactions. Teller duties often involve handling cash, counting money, and verifying customer identification. They also provide general customer service and answer basic inquiries about accounts.\n\nOn the other hand, a banker typically has a broader range of responsibilities and is involved in more complex financial transactions. Bankers often work in a more advisory role, assisting customers with opening new accounts, applying for loans, and providing financial advice. They may also be responsible for cross-selling bank products and services, such as credit cards or investment accounts. Bankers typically have a deeper understanding of financial products and services and may require additional training or certifications.\n\nIn summary, tellers primarily handle basic transactions and provide general customer service, while bankers have a more comprehensive role that involves advising customers on various financial matters.	204	35c40160-e9ba-4096-b87a-ad99317eee94	1
