d45dea90-edea-464c-9016-816393d4e4ef	assistant	2023-12-03 10:46:15.777812	While there is no universally agreed-upon set of standards for professional development specifically for international ELT secondary school teachers, there are several frameworks and guidelines that can inform and guide their professional development. These frameworks often focus on broader teaching standards and competencies that can be applied to various teaching contexts, including international ELT secondary schools. Here are a few examples:\n\n1. TESOL Professional Standards: The TESOL International Association has developed a set of professional standards for English language teachers. These standards cover various aspects of teaching, including language, culture, planning, instruction, assessment, and professionalism. While not specific to international ELT secondary schools, these standards provide a comprehensive framework for professional development in the field.\n\n2. Cambridge English Teaching Framework: Cambridge English has developed a teaching framework that outlines the knowledge, skills, and competencies required for effective English language teaching. This framework covers areas such as planning and preparing lessons, managing the classroom, assessing learning, and developing professionally. It can serve as a guide for professional development for international ELT secondary school teachers.\n\n3. British Council Continuing Professional Development Framework: The British Council has developed a framework for continuing professional development (CPD) for English language teachers. This framework focuses on four key areas: knowledge, skills, values, and reflection. It provides guidance on how teachers can develop their expertise and improve their teaching practice through ongoing professional development.\n\n4. IATEFL Teacher Development Framework: The International Association of Teachers of English as a Foreign Language (IATEFL) has developed a teacher development framework that outlines the key areas of professional development for English language teachers. This framework covers areas such as language awareness, teaching skills, professional relationships, and reflective practice. It can be used as a guide for professional development for international ELT secondary school teachers.\n\nWhile these frameworks provide valuable guidance, it is important to adapt and contextualize them to the specific needs and challenges of international ELT secondary school teachers. Teachers and institutions can use these frameworks as a starting point and customize their professional development plans to meet the unique requirements of their teaching context. Additionally, seeking input from colleagues, mentors, and professional organizations can further inform and enhance professional development efforts.	437	7f418a90-88b9-4792-9c65-20481db96beb	1
