34d0a0b4-425c-481c-8df1-f868636663e1	assistant	2023-12-04 07:58:09.910693	To find the variance in grouped frequency data, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the midpoint of each class interval. This can be done by adding the lower and upper limits of each interval and dividing by 2.\n\n2. Calculate the mean of the data set. This can be done by multiplying each midpoint by its corresponding frequency, summing up these products, and dividing by the total number of observations.\n\n3. Calculate the deviation of each midpoint from the mean. This can be done by subtracting the mean from each midpoint.\n\n4. Square each deviation obtained in step 3.\n\n5. Multiply each squared deviation by its corresponding frequency.\n\n6. Sum up all the products obtained in step 5.\n\n7. Divide the sum obtained in step 6 by the total number of observations.\n\nThe result of step 7 will give you the variance of the grouped frequency data.	177	04740c50-8a31-438d-bf31-932d4705d41f	1
