ional development activities, such as attending workshops, conferences, and webinars, participating in online communities, and engaging in action research.\n\n3. LATEFL Framework:\n   - The LATEFL Framework is a professional development framework developed by Latin American Teachers of English as a Foreign Language (LATEFL), an organization that promotes the professional development of ELT teachers in Latin America.\n   - The framework is designed to guide teachers in their professional growth and provide a roadmap for their career development.\n   - It consists of four stages: Initial, Developing, Proficient, and Expert. Each stage outlines the key competencies and skills that teachers should develop at that level.\n   - The framework emphasizes the importance of continuous learning, reflective practice, and collaboration among teachers.\n   - It encourages teachers to engage in a variety of professional development activities, such as attending conferences, workshops, and seminars, participating in online communities, and pursuing further qualifications.\n\nThese frameworks provide valuable guidance and standards for the professional development of ELT teachers. They emphasize the importance of continuous learning, reflective practice, and collaboration, and provide teachers with a roadmap for their career development. Teachers can use these frameworks to assess their own professional development needs, set goals, and plan their learning journey.	574	2783b31d-0267-429b-987b-4fff458deed3	1
