c94ba003-1d85-4ed0-8026-63c4a5a0cebf	assistant	2023-12-13 15:48:24.741175	The formula for forming the simple past tense in English is:\n\nSubject + Verb (in past tense) + Object\n\nFor regular verbs, the past tense is formed by adding -ed to the base form of the verb. For example:\n\nBase form: walk\nPast tense: walked\n\nBase form: play\nPast tense: played\n\nBase form: study\nPast tense: studied\n\nHowever, there are also many irregular verbs in English that have their own unique past tense forms. For example:\n\nBase form: go\nPast tense: went\n\nBase form: eat\nPast tense: ate\n\nBase form: see\nPast tense: saw\n\nIt's important to note that not all verbs follow the regular -ed pattern, so it's necessary to learn the past tense forms of irregular verbs individually.	160	de72389f-8328-415b-a38f-edcd23b3b546	1
