da5d3569-a5a1-4c94-a5fc-bf6647257045	assistant	2023-12-17 10:41:35.211306	Background:\nEnglish as a Foreign Language (EFL) education plays a crucial role in Ethiopia, particularly in government secondary schools in Addis Ababa City Administration. The quality of EFL instruction depends on the professional development of teachers. However, there is limited research on the perceptions, practices, and challenges of EFL teachers' professional development in this context. Understanding these factors is essential for improving the quality of EFL education and supporting teachers in their professional growth.\n\nStatement of the Problem:\nThe professional development of EFL teachers is vital for enhancing their teaching skills, updating their knowledge, and keeping up with the latest pedagogical approaches. However, there is a lack of comprehensive research on the perceptions, practices, and challenges of EFL teachers' professional development in government secondary schools in Addis Ababa City Administration. This knowledge gap hinders the development of effective professional development programs and policies tailored to the specific needs of EFL teachers in this context.\n\nScope:\nThis study focuses on government secondary schools in Addis Ababa City Administration, specifically examining the perceptions, practices, and challenges of EFL teachers' professional development. The study will involve a sample of EFL teachers from selected schools within the city administration.\n\nSignificance:\nThe findings of this study will contribute to the existing body of knowledge on EFL teachers' professional development in Ethiopia, specifically in government secondary schools in Addis Ababa City Administration. The study will provide insights into the perceptions of EFL teachers regarding the importance and effectiveness of professional development, the current practices of professional development, and the challenges faced by EFL teachers in their professional growth. The results will inform policymakers, school administrators, and teacher educators in designing and implementing effective professional development programs that address the specific needs and challenges of EFL teachers in this context. Ultimately, this research aims to improve the quality of EFL education and support the professional growth of EFL teachers in government secondary schools in Addis Ababa City Administration.	391	b2711555-ef0b-403e-b609-3a585f991501	1
