d68c209b-9378-46bf-9dfe-6389325ffbea	assistant	2023-12-17 10:52:25.951146	Research Design:\nThe research design for this PhD thesis is a mixed-methods approach, combining both quantitative and qualitative methods. This allows for a comprehensive exploration of EFL teachers' professional development, including their perceptions, practices, and challenges.\n\nMethodology:\nThe methodology for this study involves collecting data from EFL teachers in selected government secondary schools in Addis Ababa City Administration. The data collection methods include surveys, interviews, and observations. The surveys provide quantitative data on teachers' perceptions and practices, while the interviews and observations offer qualitative insights into their experiences and challenges.\n\nMethods:\n1. Surveys: A structured questionnaire will be developed to collect quantitative data on EFL teachers' perceptions and practices of professional development. The survey will include Likert-scale and multiple-choice questions to gather data on various aspects of professional development.\n\n2. Interviews: Semi-structured interviews will be conducted with a subset of EFL teachers to gain in-depth qualitative insights into their experiences, perceptions, and challenges related to professional development. The interviews will be audio-recorded and transcribed for analysis.\n\n3. Observations: Classroom observations will be conducted to observe the actual practices of EFL teachers during their professional development activities. This will provide additional qualitative data on the implementation and effectiveness of professional development practices.\n\nTools:\n1. Questionnaire: A structured questionnaire will be developed to collect quantitative data. The questionnaire will include Likert-scale and multiple-choice questions related to EFL teachers' perceptions and practices of professional development.\n\n2. Interview guide: A semi-structured interview guide will be developed to conduct interviews with a subset of EFL teachers. The interview guide will include open-ended questions to explore their experiences, perceptions, and challenges in more depth.\n\nSampling:\nThe sampling for this study will involve selecting government secondary schools in Addis Ababa City Administration. A purposive sampling technique will be used to select schools that represent a range of characteristics, such as location, student population, and resources. Within each selected school, a convenience sampling technique will be used to select EFL teachers who will participate in the study.\n\nSampling Techniques:\n1. Purposive Sampling: This technique will be used to select government secondary schools in Addis Ababa City Administration that represent a range of characteristics.\n\n2. Convenience Sampling: Within each selected school, EFL teachers will be conveniently sampled based on their availability and willingness to participate in the study.\n\nData Analysis:\nThe data analysis for this study will involve both quantitative and qualitative analysis techniques.\n\n1. Quantitative Analysis: The quantitative data collected through surveys will be analyzed using descriptive statistics, such as frequencies, percentages, and means. Inferential statistics, such as correlation and regression analysis, may also be used to examine relationships between variables.\n\n2. Qualitative Analysis: The qualitative data collected through interviews and observations will be analyzed using thematic analysis. Transcripts and field notes will be coded and categorized into themes and sub-themes to identify patterns and trends in EFL teachers' experiences and challenges.\n\nValidity and Reliability:\nTo ensure the validity and reliability of the study, several measures will be taken. The survey questionnaire and interview guide will be pilot-tested with a small group of EFL teachers to assess their clarity and appropriateness. The researcher will also establish trustworthiness by maintaining a reflexive stance, using multiple data sources, and employing member checking to validate the findings.\n\nEthical Procedures:\nEthical considerations will be followed throughout the research process. Informed consent will be obtained from all participants, and their confidentiality and anonymity will be ensured. The research will adhere to ethical guidelines and regulations set by the university and relevant authorities.\n\nSampling Frame:\nThe sampling frame for this study is government secondary schools in Addis Ababa City Administration. The specific schools will be selected based on their characteristics and availability for participation in the study.	763	b2711555-ef0b-403e-b609-3a585f991501	1
