81ef8699-59ae-4013-b3f2-72818624ef99	assistant	2023-12-17 17:38:31.167691	Constitutionalism is a political philosophy and system of governance that emphasizes the importance of a written constitution as the supreme law of the land. It is based on the idea that government power should be limited and constrained by a set of fundamental principles and rules outlined in the constitution. Constitutionalism promotes the rule of law, separation of powers, protection of individual rights, and accountability of the government to its citizens. It ensures that the government operates within the boundaries set by the constitution and respects the rights and freedoms of its citizens.	104	41e03953-b4c2-4a99-97fa-316c6d02b46d	1
