ndicating linear time complexity. This means that the running time of the program grows linearly with the input size `n`.\n\nBy following this process, you can count the number of operations and determine the time complexity of a Java program. Remember that this is an approximation and provides an upper bound on the growth rate of the algorithm. The actual running time may vary depending on various factors.	469	0fc1e0da-17df-4fbd-b99d-c9f494277d5d	1
