e488bec4-2c28-4344-b85c-844fdb124633	assistant	2023-12-23 19:13:19.941171	To create a Zoom meeting link that can be accessed via HTTP, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Sign in to your Zoom account on the Zoom website (zoom.us).\n2. Click on the "Schedule a Meeting" button on the top right corner of the page.\n3. Fill in the details for your meeting, such as the topic, date, time, and duration.\n4. Under the "Meeting Options" section, make sure the "Require meeting password" option is unchecked if you want to allow participants to join without a password.\n5. Scroll down to the "Video" section and choose whether you want the host and participants' video to be on or off when joining the meeting.\n6. Scroll further down to the "Meeting ID" section and select the "Generate Automatically" option.\n7. In the "Meeting Options" section, make sure the "Enable join from your browser" option is checked. This will allow participants to join the meeting via a web browser without needing to download the Zoom app.\n8. Once you have filled in all the necessary details, click on the "Save" button at the bottom of the page.\n9. After saving, you will be redirected to the meeting details page. Here, you will find the HTTP Zoom meeting link under the "Join Zoom Meeting" section. It will look something like this: "https://zoom.us/j/1234567890".\n\nYou can copy this link and share it with your participants via email, messaging apps, or any other communication method. They can simply click on the link to join the Zoom meeting using their web browser.	325	6a9945c6-3fb1-4ecd-b4d2-16d693eb3cf5	1
