7b00e90e-c76b-4ee9-9468-af616917e376	assistant	2024-01-16 08:03:27.829173	Title: Changing Active Voice to Passive Voice: A Simple Guide\n\nIntroduction:\nHello everyone! Today, I will guide you through the process of changing active voice to passive voice in a simple and easy-to-understand way. We will cover the present, past, and future tenses. Let's get started!\n\nI. Present Tense:\nTo change active voice to passive voice in the present tense, follow this formula:\n\nSubject + am/is/are + past participle + (by + agent)\n\nExample:\nActive Voice: The cat chases the mouse.\nPassive Voice: The mouse is chased by the cat.\n\nNote: You can include the agent (the doer of the action) using the preposition "by."\n\nII. Past Tense:\nTo change active voice to passive voice in the past tense, use this formula:\n\nSubject + was/were + past participle + (by + agent)\n\nExample:\nActive Voice: The teacher taught the students.\nPassive Voice: The students were taught by the teacher.\n\nNote: Use the past tense of the verb "to be" (was/were) followed by the past participle of the main verb.\n\nIII. Future Tense:\nTo change active voice to passive voice in the future tense, follow this formula:\n\nSubject + will/shall + be + past participle + (by + agent)\n\nExample:\nActive Voice: The company will launch a new product.\nPassive Voice: A new product will be launched by the company.\n\nNote: Use the auxiliary verb "will/shall" to indicate the future tense, followed by "be" and the past participle of the main verb. Include the agent using the preposition "by."\n\nConclusion:\nChanging active voice to passive voice is simple once you understand the formulas for each tense. By following these guidelines, you can transform your sentences effortlessly. Remember to pay attention to verb conjugation and include the agent, if necessary.\n\nThank you for your attention. I hope this simplified guide has been helpful. If you have any questions, feel free to ask.	416	06983d52-819d-4a22-94b6-9