9d117349-e88a-4fbd-bcf1-6931e702aeb5	Environmental Hazards \n Environmental hazards can also be classified into three interrelated categories \n(biological, chemical, and physical) based on the properties of their causes. These categories \nare not mutually exclusive with traditional versus modern hazards. \n For most of human history, biological hazards were the most significant factor in \nhealth. Biological hazards are infectious or communicable diseases caused by pathogens: \ndisease-causing organisms or infectious particles, such as bacteria, fungi, parasitic worms, \nprotozoa, viruses, and prions. Bacteria are single-celled organisms with small, simple cells. \nExamples of bacterial diseases include tuberculosis, cholera, bacterial pneumonia, and \ndysentery. \n Chemical hazards are toxic substances, which cause damage to living organisms. Air \npollutants (such as secondhand smoke or carbon monoxide), heavy metals, and pesticides \nare a few examples. We can be exposed to these contaminants from a variety of residential, \ncommercial, and industrial sources. Sometimes harmful environmental contaminants occur \nbiologically, such as those from mold or a toxic algae bloom. Toxins can be classified based \non their origin, purpose, chemical structure and properties, or effects. \n Physical hazards are additional forces that can imperil humans. Physical hazards may \narise naturally such as natural disasters (earthquakes, wildfires, landslides, etc.) or extreme \nweather. Others may arise from human structures or activities (traffic accident, building \ncollapse, injury from mechanical equipment, strain on the body from repeated movements, \netc.) Some physical hazards, such as explosions or radiation, can arise from natural or human \nsources. \nInstruction 01:Answer the following \nquestions \n1.What kind of expository writing is the \npassage? \n2.Use the outlining method to analyze the \npassage? \n3.Write a short summary of the above \npassage? \n4.Use a mind map to show the relationship \nbetween the ideas? \nInstruction 02:Vocabulary Section \n1.Guess the meaning of the words in bold. \nA. interrelated \nB. Infectious \nC. Pathogens \nD. Imperil \nE. Arise	2023-11-11 13:55:13.016433	f	\N	0	703a5185-2e98-470e-90c4-a24557de800d	\N	630ca76a-9c8a-4808-a77f-ab38fe9a209f	2023-11-16 10:05:28.85527
