eb84e572-a653-45b3-a859-e0d4241cfaa0	Guide Reviewing Research Articles\nHere are some things you should consider as you review the article of your choice.  \n1) a) What is the purpose of this article? b) Is the problem statement clearly stated? c) Please indicate the gap which is substantiated in the article, d) Why is it important to investigate or examine the subject of the article?  \n2) a) What are the main research questions or hypotheses of the article? b) Are they logical to the gap that is indicated in the article? c) What significance is substantiated in the study? \n3) a) Is the literature review adequate in your opinion; theoretical, empirical and conceptual framework? b)  In your opinion what has come out of the literature review in the article? \n4) a) Are the methods appropriate and adequate to the task?, b) Give your assessment on the research methodology of the study, c) Do you think that the method applied in the article is also replicable in other contexts? Give your justifications; d) is the operationalization and measurement of the variables clear?  \n 5) a) Are the findings clearly stated? b) How does this advance knowledge in the field? c) Does the results indicated in the article linked to the research objective, questions/hypotheses? d) Explain and give us concrete examples from the research findings of the article. \n6) Give your overall critical comment on the relevance of the study as indicated in the article; the problem selected, the methodology followed and the findings, conclusion drawn and recommendation suggested. \nRequirements and deadline \n1)  Google/ search a recent article which is published since 2018 G.C related with topics in the areas of strategic Management, review results following the above guide in Ms Word with maximum six pages.\n2)  It is strictly not allowed to use one article by more than one Group.\n3)  Copy & plagiarism will critically be detected, so rely on your work only.	2023-09-21 10:48:25.994153	f	\N	0	de3eb